================================================================================
ADAPTATION AND CREDITS
================================================================================

actdocs-rs is an independent reimplementation, in Rust, of actdocs:

    actdocs
    https://github.com/tmknom/actdocs
    Copyright tmknom
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0

The reference used was actdocs v0.6.1. Upstream ships no NOTICE file, so there
are no upstream attribution notices to carry forward; what follows is offered as
credit rather than to discharge an obligation.

No Go source code was copied or mechanically translated. The Rust implementation
was written against a behavioural specification derived from reading the
upstream source and its golden tests. What was deliberately reproduced is the
observable output contract, so that a document generated by either tool can be
regenerated by the other without churn:

  - the section headings "## Description", "## Inputs", "## Secrets",
    "## Outputs" and "## Permissions"
  - the table headers, alignment rows and column order of each section
  - the placeholders "n/a", "N/A", "yes" and "no", and the distinction between
    a value that is absent and one that is present but empty
  - the folding of multi-line values into "<pre>" ... "<br>" ... "</pre>"
  - the marker directives "<!-- actdocs start -->" and "<!-- actdocs end -->"
  - the JSON shape emitted by "generate --format=json"
  - ordering: required entries first, then by name within each group

actdocs-rs also diverges from upstream deliberately in a number of places, and
adds a "sync" command with no upstream equivalent. Those differences are
enumerated in README.md.

================================================================================
PRIOR ART
================================================================================

The "sync" pipeline -- scaffolding a document, replacing marked regions, the
usage snippet and the repository index -- began as a Bash and jq wrapper around
actdocs, "scripts/generate-action-docs.sh". actdocs-rs absorbs that pipeline and
replaces both it and its dependency on actdocs and jq.
